export default {
  title: "DATA RETENTION POLICY",
  pageLabel: "Data Retention Policy",
  currentPath: "/data-retention",
  paragraphs: [
  "THIS DATA RETENTION POLICY is made available by DataDost, a financial clarity platform accessible at datadost.in, and having its email address at Legal@datadost.in, hereinafter referred to as \"DataDost\", which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, be deemed to mean and include its successors-in-interest, administrators, and permitted assigns.",
  "WHEREAS DataDost operates an interactive, web-based financial document analysis and financial clarity platform, hereinafter referred to as the \"Platform\", which allows Users to upload financial documents such as bank statements, salary slips, credit card statements, and other financial records, and to ask questions in plain language about the data contained in those documents;",
  "AND WHEREAS in the course of operating the Platform, DataDost collects and processes certain Personal Data of Users, and DataDost acts as the Data Fiduciary for all Personal Data collected through the Platform;",
  "AND WHEREAS DataDost processes such Personal Data in accordance with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, hereinafter referred to as the \"DPDP Act\", and the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025, hereinafter referred to as the \"DPDP Rules\";",
  "AND WHEREAS DataDost engages Anthropic PBC, the provider of the Claude application programming interface, hereinafter referred to as the \"Claude API\", as a Data Processor, and Anthropic PBC processes the text extracted from Documents on infrastructure located outside India, and the retention of such data by Anthropic PBC is governed by Anthropic PBC's own retention practices;",
  "AND WHEREAS DataDost wishes to set out the categories of Personal Data collected by it through the Platform, the purpose for which each category is processed, the legal basis for processing, the retention period applicable to each category, and the deletion or anonymisation procedure followed at the end of that period;",
  "AND WHEREAS this Data Retention Policy is to be read together with the Privacy Policy, the Terms of Service, the User Data Processing Consent, and the Refund Policy, each of which is available on the Platform, and in the event of any inconsistency between this Data Retention Policy and the Privacy Policy or the Terms of Service, the Privacy Policy and the Terms of Service shall prevail to the extent of the inconsistency, and this Data Retention Policy shall be construed so as to give effect to the Privacy Policy and the Terms of Service;",
  "NOW, THEREFORE, DataDost sets out this Data Retention Policy as follows:",
  "For the purposes of this Data Retention Policy, unless the context otherwise requires or admits of a different interpretation, the following terms and expressions shall have the meanings ascribed to them herein below. The term \"DataDost\" shall mean and include the operator of the DataDost platform accessible at datadost.in, and its successors-in-interest, administrators, and permitted assigns. The term \"Platform\" shall mean and include the interactive financial document analysis and financial clarity platform operated by DataDost, including the website at datadost.in, the mobile-responsive web application, the backend systems, the document parsing engine, the AI query interface, the tax regime comparison engine, the EMI affordability calculator, the spending categorisation engine, and all related technology, software, and services provided by DataDost. The term \"User\" shall mean and include any individual who accesses, uploads a document to, or uses the DataDost Platform, including but not limited to any person who uploads a bank statement, salary slip, credit card statement, or other financial document, asks a question through the Platform, or attempts to use any feature offered through the Platform. The term \"Document\" shall mean and include any bank statement, salary slip, credit card statement, or other financial record uploaded by the User to the Platform. The term \"Anthropic\" shall mean and include Anthropic PBC, a company incorporated in the United States of America, and the provider of the Claude API. The term \"Claude API\" shall mean and include the application programming interface provided by Anthropic through which DataDost transmits the text extracted from Documents for the purpose of generating responses to User queries. The term \"AI Processing Service\" shall mean and include Anthropic, and any successor or assign of Anthropic that continues to provide the Claude API or a substantially similar service, and Anthropic is the AI Processing Service engaged by DataDost for the purposes of this Data Retention Policy. The term \"Data Processing Addendum\" shall mean and include the written agreement between DataDost and Anthropic that governs the processing of Personal Data by Anthropic on behalf of DataDost, and that imposes on Anthropic obligations no less restrictive than those imposed on DataDost under the Data Protection Laws. The term \"Personal Data\" shall have the meaning ascribed to it under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and shall include any data about an individual who is identifiable by or in relation to such data. The term \"Data Fiduciary\" shall have the meaning ascribed to it under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and shall mean DataDost. The term \"Data Principal\" shall have the meaning ascribed to it under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and shall mean the User. The term \"Data Processor\" shall have the meaning ascribed to it under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and shall include any person who processes Personal Data on behalf of the Data Fiduciary, including Anthropic in respect of the Claude API, the hosting provider, the authentication provider, the email provider, the messaging provider, and the payment processor. The term \"Data Protection Laws\" shall mean and include the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and the rules and regulations made thereunder, as amended from time to time, and any other applicable data protection or privacy laws in force in India. The term \"Processing Log\" shall mean and include any record of the processing activities carried out by DataDost or by any Data Processor on behalf of DataDost. The term \"Aggregated Data\" shall mean and include statistical information from which identifying fields have been removed, so that no individual is identifiable, and Aggregated Data is not personal data and is not subject to the provisions of this Data Retention Policy. The term \"Data Protection Officer\" shall mean and include the officer appointed by DataDost under Section 10 of the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, being Santosh Dave, whose email address is privacy@datadost.in. The term \"Grievance Officer\" shall mean and include the officer appointed by DataDost under the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, whose email address is grievance@datadost.in. The headings and titles inserted in this Data Retention Policy, if any, are for convenience of reference only and shall not affect the construction or interpretation of this Data Retention Policy, and words importing the singular shall include the plural and vice versa, and words importing any gender shall include all genders. The word \"including\" or \"includes\" shall be construed as \"including without limitation\" or \"includes without limitation\", and shall not be construed to limit the generality of any preceding words.",
  "This Data Retention Policy sets out the categories of Personal Data collected by DataDost through the Platform, the purpose for which each category is processed, the legal basis for processing, the retention period applicable to each category, and the deletion or anonymisation procedure followed at the end of that period. This Data Retention Policy is issued in accordance with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025. This Data Retention Policy is to be read together with the Privacy Policy and the Terms of Service, and in the event of any inconsistency between this Data Retention Policy and the Privacy Policy or the Terms of Service, the Privacy Policy and the Terms of Service shall prevail to the extent of the inconsistency, and this Data Retention Policy shall be construed so as to give effect to the Privacy Policy and the Terms of Service. DataDost retains Personal Data only for as long as is necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected, and erases or anonymises such Personal Data when the purpose for which it was collected is fulfilled, or when the User withdraws consent, subject to any legal requirement to retain it for a longer period. DataDost does not retain Personal Data for any longer than is necessary for the purposes set out in this Data Retention Policy, the Privacy Policy, and the Terms of Service.",
  "DataDost collects the User's account identifier from the authentication provider when the User signs in. The purpose of processing the account identifier is to identify the User and to provide access to the Platform. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. The account identifier is retained for twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform, and is then permanently removed. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the account identifier or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable. The account identifier is processed by DataDost on servers located in India, and by the authentication provider on infrastructure that may be located outside India. Where the authentication provider is Google, the identity verification exchange occurs on Google's infrastructure, which may involve a cross-border transfer, and the User acknowledges and agrees that DataDost does not control Google's retention practices in respect of that processing. Where the authentication provider is any other provider, the same principle applies, and DataDost does not control the retention practices of that provider in respect of the identity verification exchange.",
  "DataDost collects the User's email address from the authentication provider when the User signs in. The purpose of processing the email address is to communicate with the User, to identify the User, to send the User notices required under the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules, and to send the User results emails and marketing communications if the User has separately agreed to receive them. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent, and, in respect of notices required under the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules, the legal basis is DataDost's legal obligation. The email address is retained for twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform, and is then permanently removed. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the email address or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable. Where the User has separately agreed to receive marketing communications, the email address shall be retained for the purpose of sending such communications until the User unsubscribes, and upon unsubscribe, the email address shall be retained only for the purpose of maintaining a suppression list, so that DataDost does not send further marketing communications to the User. DataDost shall not use the email address for any purpose other than the purposes set out in this Data Retention Policy and in the Privacy Policy.",
  "DataDost collects the User's display name from the authentication provider when the User signs in. The purpose of processing the display name is to personalise the User's experience on the Platform. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. The display name is retained for twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform, and is then permanently removed. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the display name or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable.",
  "DataDost collects the User's phone number if the User chooses to sign in using a one-time password via SMS or WhatsApp. The purpose of processing the phone number is to authenticate the User and to deliver the one-time password. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. The phone number is retained for twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform, and is then permanently removed. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the phone number or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable. Where the User signs in with a one-time password over WhatsApp, the phone number is processed by Meta Platforms, Inc. and its affiliates on infrastructure outside India for the sole purpose of delivering that message, and DataDost does not control the retention practices of Meta Platforms, Inc. in respect of that processing. The User acknowledges and agrees that the transmission of the phone number to Meta Platforms, Inc. for the purpose of delivering the one-time password involves a cross-border transfer of Personal Data, and that DataDost has disclosed this transfer to the User in the Privacy Policy and in the Terms of Service.",
  "DataDost collects the Documents uploaded by the User, including bank statements, salary slips, credit card statements, and other financial records, and the text and numerical data extracted from those Documents. The purpose of processing the Documents and the extracted text is to provide the core service, being the analysis of the User's financial documents, and to generate responses to the User's queries. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. The Documents and the extracted text are retained on DataDost's own systems for thirty (30) days from the date of processing, and are then cleared. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the Documents and the extracted text or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable. DataDost shall inform the User at least forty-eight (48) hours before erasing the Documents and the extracted text because the purpose for which they were collected has been fulfilled, giving the User a final opportunity to exercise their rights under the DPDP Act. This notice is required under Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025, and DataDost shall send it to the email address associated with the User's account. If the User does not respond to the notice within forty-eight (48) hours, DataDost shall proceed with the erasure of the Documents and the extracted text in accordance with this Data Retention Policy. DataDost does not store the User's PAN, Aadhaar, or any other government-issued identification number, and where such numbers appear in a Document uploaded by the User, DataDost does not display them back to the User and does not retain them beyond the period described in this paragraph. DataDost does not store the Documents uploaded by the User on its own servers beyond the period described in this paragraph, and the Documents are read in memory and the extracted text is transmitted to Anthropic through the Claude API for the purpose of generating responses to the User's queries.",
  "DataDost collects the User's query history and the output generated in response to those queries. The purpose of processing the query history and the output is to provide the core service and to allow the User to review past queries during the retention period. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. The query history and the output are retained on DataDost's own systems for thirty (30) days from the date of processing, and are then cleared. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the query history and the output or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable. DataDost shall inform the User at least forty-eight (48) hours before erasing the query history and the output because the purpose for which they were collected has been fulfilled, giving the User a final opportunity to exercise their rights under the DPDP Act. This notice is required under Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025, and DataDost shall send it to the email address associated with the User's account. If the User does not respond to the notice within forty-eight (48) hours, DataDost shall proceed with the erasure of the query history and the output in accordance with this Data Retention Policy.",
  "DataDost collects the User's consent records, including the User's consent to data processing, AI processing, results emails, and marketing communications, along with the version of the notice the User agreed to, the date and time of the consent, and the manner in which the consent was given. The purpose of processing the consent records is to demonstrate compliance with the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules, and to establish that the User gave free, specific, informed, and unambiguous consent to the processing of the User's Personal Data. The legal basis for processing is DataDost's legal obligation under the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules. The consent records are retained for twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform, and are then retained without identifying fields. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall remove the identifying fields from the consent records, so that no individual is identifiable, while retaining the consent record itself for the purpose of demonstrating compliance with the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules. The User acknowledges and agrees that the retention of consent records without identifying fields is necessary for DataDost to demonstrate compliance with the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules, and that this retention does not infringe any right of the User under the DPDP Act.",
  "DataDost collects processing logs, including records of the processing activities carried out by DataDost and by Anthropic on behalf of DataDost, records of the categories of Personal Data processed, records of the purposes for which the Personal Data was processed, records of the recipients to whom the Personal Data was disclosed, records of any cross-border transfers of Personal Data, and records of any Personal Data Breach that occurred. The purpose of processing the processing logs is to demonstrate compliance with the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules and for security purposes. The legal basis for processing is DataDost's legal obligation under the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules. The processing logs are retained for twelve (12) months from the date of processing, and are then retained without identifying fields. Under Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025, DataDost retains processing logs for a minimum of one (1) year from the date of processing, even where deletion of Personal Data is requested. These logs are retained without identifying fields attached to them. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall remove the identifying fields from the processing logs, so that no individual is identifiable, while retaining the processing log itself for the purpose of demonstrating compliance with the DPDP Act and the DPDP Rules. The User acknowledges and agrees that the retention of processing logs for a minimum of one (1) year is required by Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025, and that this retention does not infringe any right of the User under the DPDP Act.",
  "DataDost collects the User's IP address and full browser user-agent string automatically when the User accesses the Platform. The purpose of processing the IP address and the user agent is to ensure the security of the Platform, to detect and prevent abuse, fraud, and security incidents, and to comply with legal and regulatory obligations. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent, and, in respect of security and compliance purposes, DataDost's legitimate use under the DPDP Act. The IP address and the user agent are retained for twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform, and are then permanently removed. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall either delete the IP address and the user agent or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable.",
  "DataDost collects behavioural and activity records, including which screens the User reaches, the timestamps of the User's activities, the time taken per query, and the placement identifier, being the unique code on any physical card or seat-back plate the User scanned, if applicable. The purpose of processing the behavioural and activity records is to improve the Platform and the user experience using only Aggregated Data, and to detect and prevent abuse, fraud, and security incidents. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent, and, in respect of the improvement of the Platform, DataDost's legitimate use under the DPDP Act. The behavioural and activity records are retained as counts, with identifiers cleared at twelve (12) months from the date of the User's last use of the Platform. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall remove the identifying fields from the behavioural and activity records, so that no individual is identifiable, while retaining the counts for the purpose of improving the Platform and the user experience and for the purpose of detecting and preventing abuse, fraud, and security incidents. The User acknowledges and agrees that the retention of behavioural and activity records as counts, without identifying fields, is necessary for DataDost to improve the Platform and to detect and prevent abuse, fraud, and security incidents, and that this retention does not infringe any right of the User under the DPDP Act.",
  "DataDost collects session data when the User accesses the Platform. The purpose of processing the session data is to maintain the User's session and to provide access to the Platform. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. The session store is retained for two (2) hours of inactivity. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall delete the session data. The session data is stored in a first-party cookie, and does not carry Personal Data. The session cookie follows the session lifetime, which is two hours of inactivity rather than the close of the browser.",
  "DataDost collects payment records, including the User's transaction identifier, the amount paid, the date of payment, and the status of the payment, when the User subscribes to a paid plan. The purpose of processing the payment records is to process the Subscription Fee, to provide access to the paid features of the Platform, to comply with applicable tax and accounting laws, and to resolve any payment-related disputes. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent and DataDost's legal obligation under applicable tax and accounting laws. The payment records are retained for the period required by applicable tax and accounting laws, which is currently eight (8) years from the end of the relevant financial year. When the retention period expires, DataDost shall delete the payment records. DataDost does not store the User's full card number, card verification value, or any other sensitive payment credential, and all such information is processed by the Payment Processor in accordance with the Payment Processor's own privacy policy and applicable law. The User acknowledges and agrees that the retention of payment records for the period required by applicable tax and accounting laws is required by law, and that this retention does not infringe any right of the User under the DPDP Act.",
  "DataDost transmits the text extracted from the User's Documents to Anthropic through the Claude API for the purpose of generating responses to the User's queries. The purpose of processing the extracted text is to generate responses to the User's queries. The legal basis for processing is the User's consent. Anthropic's standard retention period for inputs and outputs transmitted through the Claude API is thirty (30) days from the date of receipt or generation, after which the inputs and outputs are automatically deleted from Anthropic's backend, unless a longer retention period applies as described in the following sentences. If the data is flagged by Anthropic's automated trust and safety systems as a violation of Anthropic's Usage Policy, Anthropic retains the inputs and outputs for up to two (2) years from the date of the flag. Anthropic retains trust and safety classification scores for up to seven (7) years from the date of the classification, irrespective of whether the underlying inputs and outputs are retained for the full two-year period. Anthropic may also retain inputs and outputs for longer where it is required to do so by law, or where it is necessary to enforce Anthropic's Usage Policy or to address violations of Anthropic's terms of service. Anthropic does not use the inputs and outputs transmitted through the Claude API to train its models, and Anthropic has contractually agreed, in the Data Processing Addendum between DataDost and Anthropic, that it shall not use the User's Personal Data for any purpose other than providing the Claude API services to DataDost. DataDost does not have the technical ability to delete data from Anthropic's backend before the expiry of the retention periods described in this paragraph, because the Claude API does not offer an API endpoint for the deletion of individual records. DataDost's obligation under Section 8(8) of the DPDP Act to ensure that the Data Processor erases Personal Data upon instruction is fulfilled to the extent possible by the contractual terms of the Data Processing Addendum and by the automatic deletion periods described in this paragraph. DataDost cannot override Anthropic's internal trust and safety retention periods. DataDost has disclosed these retention periods to the User in the Privacy Policy and in the Terms of Service, and the User's consent to the processing of the User's Personal Data includes consent to these retention periods. The User acknowledges and agrees that the extracted text from any Document uploaded by the User may be transmitted to Anthropic, may be processed on infrastructure located outside India, and may be retained by Anthropic for the periods described in this paragraph, and that DataDost has disclosed these periods to the User.",
  "When the retention period for a category of Personal Data expires, DataDost shall either delete the data or remove the identifying fields from the data, so that no individual is identifiable. When the User requests deletion of their Personal Data, DataDost shall remove the identifying fields from its own systems and shall instruct Anthropic to do the same, to the extent technically possible. Anthropic's automatic deletion periods described in this Data Retention Policy shall apply. DataDost shall inform the User at least forty-eight (48) hours before erasing the User's Personal Data because the purpose for which it was collected has been fulfilled, giving the User a final opportunity to exercise their rights under the DPDP Act. This notice is required under Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025, and DataDost shall send it to the email address associated with the User's account. If the User does not respond to the notice within forty-eight (48) hours, DataDost shall proceed with the erasure of the User's Personal Data in accordance with this Data Retention Policy. DataDost shall retain processing logs for a minimum of one (1) year from the date of processing, even where deletion of Personal Data is requested, in accordance with Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025. Where the User has withdrawn consent, or has requested erasure, any Document uploaded by the User and any output generated in response to the User's queries shall cease to be accessible at the time the request takes effect, subject to the retention periods applicable to Anthropic as described in this Data Retention Policy. The User acknowledges and agrees that the withdrawal of consent does not affect the lawfulness of any processing carried out before the withdrawal, and that the withdrawal of consent does not entitle the User to a refund of any portion of the Subscription Fee already paid, and that the User's right to a refund is governed solely by the Refund Policy.",
  "DataDost's nightly database dumps are retained for approximately one (1) week, and infrastructure snapshots for four (4) weeks. A person erased today persists in backups for up to four (4) weeks. DataDost shall take all reasonable steps to ensure that Personal Data in backups is not accessed, processed, or disclosed except for the purpose of restoring DataDost's systems in the event of a failure, and shall delete or anonymise such Personal Data as soon as practicable after the backup is restored or the retention period for the backup expires. DataDost shall not use any Personal Data in backups for any purpose other than restoring DataDost's systems in the event of a failure. The User acknowledges and agrees that the existence of Personal Data in backups for a limited period after erasure is a technical necessity, and that DataDost has taken reasonable steps to ensure that such Personal Data is not accessed, processed, or disclosed for any purpose other than restoring DataDost's systems in the event of a failure.",
  "DataDost's application servers and database backups are located in India. However, the User acknowledges and agrees that the extracted text transmitted to Anthropic is processed on infrastructure located outside India, that the identity verification exchange carried out by the authentication provider may occur on infrastructure located outside India, and that where the User signs in with a one-time password over WhatsApp, the User's phone number is processed by Meta Platforms, Inc. and its affiliates on infrastructure outside India for the sole purpose of delivering that message. The User acknowledges and agrees that these cross-border transfers of Personal Data are necessary for the operation of the Platform, and that DataDost has disclosed these transfers to the User in the Privacy Policy and in the Terms of Service. DataDost ensures that any cross-border transfer of Personal Data is subject to appropriate safeguards as required under applicable Data Protection Laws, including by entering into contractual arrangements with the recipients of the data that require them to provide a level of protection to the data that is no less than the level of protection required under the DPDP Act, and by entering into the Data Processing Addendum with Anthropic. The User consents to such transfers, subject to compliance with applicable Data Protection Laws, by consenting to the Privacy Policy and by using the Platform. Where the User does not wish the User's Personal Data to be transferred outside India, the User should not use the Platform, and should not upload any Document to the Platform.",
  "DataDost has appointed a Data Protection Officer who is responsible for overseeing the protection of the User's personal data and for addressing any questions, concerns, or complaints the User may have regarding this Data Retention Policy, the exercise of any of the User's rights under the DPDP Act, or the conduct of any Data Processor engaged by DataDost. The User may contact the Data Protection Officer at the following address: Data Protection Officer, Santosh Dave, Email: privacy@datadost.in. The Data Protection Officer will acknowledge the User's complaint within two (2) business days and will use best efforts to resolve it within fifteen (15) business days from the date of receipt. If the User is not satisfied with the response of the Data Protection Officer, the User has the right to escalate the complaint to the Data Protection Board of India, as provided under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.",
  "DataDost has also appointed a Grievance Officer who is responsible for addressing any questions, concerns, or complaints the User may have regarding the Platform, the services provided by DataDost, the Subscription, the Subscription Fee, or the refund of any Subscription Fee. The User may contact the Grievance Officer at the following address: Grievance Officer, Email: grievance@datadost.in. The Grievance Officer will acknowledge the User's complaint within two (2) business days and will use best efforts to resolve it within fifteen (15) business days from the date of receipt. If the User is not satisfied with the response of the Grievance Officer, the User has the right to escalate the complaint to the Data Protection Board of India, in respect of any matter relating to the processing of the User's Personal Data, or to the appropriate consumer forum under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, in respect of any matter relating to the Subscription or to the refund of any Subscription Fee.",
  "Where the User is uncertain as to whether a complaint should be addressed to the Data Protection Officer or to the Grievance Officer, the User may address the complaint to either officer, and that officer shall forward the complaint to the other officer if the matter falls within the other officer's remit, and shall inform the User of the forwarding, and the timelines applicable to the resolution of the complaint shall run from the date on which the complaint is received by the officer to whom it is ultimately addressed.",
  "Any questions or complaints regarding this Data Retention Policy should be addressed to the Data Protection Officer at privacy@datadost.in, or to the Grievance Officer at grievance@datadost.in, marking the message \"Grievance\". The Data Protection Officer or the Grievance Officer, as the case may be, shall acknowledge the complaint within two (2) business days and shall use best efforts to resolve it within fifteen (15) business days. If the User is not satisfied with the outcome, the User may take the matter to the Data Protection Board of India, in respect of any matter relating to the processing of the User's Personal Data, or to the appropriate consumer forum, in respect of any matter relating to the Subscription. Nothing in this Data Retention Policy limits, delays, or conditions the User's right to do so, or any other right or remedy available to the User in law. The User acknowledges and agrees that the User's right to escalate the matter to the Data Protection Board of India is without prejudice to any other right or remedy available to the User in law, and that nothing in this Data Retention Policy shall be construed as a waiver of any such right or remedy.",
  "If any provision of this Data Retention Policy is held to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, such provision shall be severed from this Data Retention Policy, and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect, and the Parties shall make a good faith effort to replace the invalid, illegal, or unenforceable provision with a valid, legal, and enforceable provision that most closely reflects the original intent of the Parties. No failure or delay by either Party in exercising any right or remedy under this Data Retention Policy shall operate as a waiver thereof, nor shall any single or partial exercise of any right or remedy preclude any other or further exercise thereof or the exercise of any other right or remedy. This Data Retention Policy constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior discussions, negotiations, agreements, and understandings, whether written or oral, between the Parties in respect of the retention of Personal Data.",
  "This Data Retention Policy is issued under, and is to be read in accordance with, the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025, the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, and the other laws in force in India which apply to it. This Data Retention Policy is a notice given by DataDost of what it does with Personal Data. It is not a contract, it creates no obligations on the User, and nothing in it requires the User's agreement in order to take effect. This Data Retention Policy shall be governed by, and construed and interpreted in accordance with, the laws of India. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Data Retention Policy shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the courts at Mumbai, Maharashtra, India, save and except that nothing in this Data Retention Policy shall take away or restrict the right of a consumer to file a complaint before the consumer forum having jurisdiction under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, whether on the basis of the consumer's place of residence, the consumer's place of work, or the place where the cause of action arises, and the jurisdiction conferred on the courts at Mumbai shall not apply to any consumer dispute, and shall not be construed as a waiver of any right or remedy available to the consumer under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. Nothing in this Data Retention Policy shall prevent the User from approaching the Data Protection Board of India in respect of any matter relating to the processing of the User's Personal Data. DataDost may amend this Data Retention Policy from time to time, and a materially amended Data Retention Policy shall be presented for acknowledgement at the User's next sign-in. DataDost shall give the User at least fifteen (15) days' prior notice of any material changes to this Data Retention Policy through the Platform or by email to the User's registered email address. The User acknowledges and agrees that it is the User's sole responsibility to review this Data Retention Policy periodically for any changes, and the User's acknowledgement of the amended Data Retention Policy at the next sign-in shall constitute the User's acknowledgement of the amended Data Retention Policy. The provisions of this Data Retention Policy relating to the retention of processing logs, the retention of consent records, the retention of payment records, the retention of data by Anthropic, the cross-border transfer of Personal Data, the deletion and anonymisation procedure, the grievance redressal mechanism, the governing law, and any other provision that by its nature is intended to survive the termination of the Terms of Service or the closure of the User's account shall survive the termination of the Terms of Service and the closure of the User's account.",
  "DataDost may be contacted for any questions, complaints, or data protection requests regarding this Data Retention Policy at the following address: DataDost, Email: privacy@datadost.in for data protection matters and for the Data Protection Officer (Santosh Dave), grievance@datadost.in for grievances relating to the Platform or the Subscription, and Legal@datadost.in for legal notices."
  ],
};
